course: dictionary
lesson: 9505
title: Reading how people speak
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone speaks or looks, not just what they do. Sternly is one of these words. It describes a voice or face that is strict and serious, with no smile.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «The teacher looked sternly over her glasses at the boy who had thrown the ball.» The teacher is not smiling, and the boy has done wrong, so sternly must mean in a strict, serious way.
explain: Stories use sternly to warn the reader that trouble is coming. In The Wind in the Willows, Badger speaks sternly to Toad about his motor cars. Always ask: would the sentence still fit if I swapped in a happy word? If not, you have found the meaning.
fact: Sternly means in a strict, serious and unsmiling way.
fact: Sternly is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something, such as speaks or looks.
fact: People often speak or look sternly when someone has done wrong.
fact: «The teacher looked sternly over her glasses.» Here the word shows that there is trouble.
exercise: «The teacher looked sternly over her glasses.» What does sternly tell you about the teacher? | *She was strict and serious | She was fast asleep | She was laughing at a joke | She was lost and confused
exercise: In The Wind in the Willows, Badger speaks sternly to Toad. What is Badger like in this part? | Shy and quiet | Excited about a party | *Serious and strict | Silly and playful
exercise: Why might a parent speak sternly? | To tell a joke | To say goodnight happily | To win a race | *To show that someone has done wrong
test: «The queen spoke sternly, and nobody in the room smiled.» What does sternly mean? | In a slow, sleepy way | In a loud, singing way | In a happy, giggly way | *In a strict, serious way
test: Which clue in «The queen spoke sternly, and nobody in the room smiled» tells you sternly means serious? | The room was very big | *Nobody in the room smiled | The queen wore a golden crown | The music was loud
exam: «The Duchess spoke sternly to Alice, and Alice felt she had done wrong.» What does sternly mean here? | Happily and kindly | Quickly and quietly | *In a strict, serious way | In a silly, playful way
